WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
Hey, look at you buying a home! That's a big step. A home is one of the most important investments

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.680
you'll ever make in your lifetime. So, way to go, you! All right, so you've gone through the

3
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:14.400
endless paperwork, signed more documents than you ever knew existed, and finally got the keys.

4
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.680
Now you're settling into your new home, and maybe it's occurred to you by now,

5
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.880
you're now in about 50 times more debt than you've ever been in before.

6
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.960
And hey, that's not a bad thing at all. Experts say mortgage debt is among the best

7
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.960
kinds of debt to have, but it is debt all the same. As long as you keep making those

8
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.240
mortgage payments on time every month, you should be good to go, right?

9
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:36.560
Here's the thing, though. There are certain events that could happen to hamper or eliminate

10
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.720
altogether your ability to keep up with those mortgage payments, leading to financial stress,

11
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:45.600
foreclosure, or even bankruptcy. It's a good idea to educate yourself about what your options

12
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.520
are to protect yourself from unforeseen circumstances. So let's do that.

13
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:55.280
Larry and Mary here are twins. At 30 years old, each of them buys a $250,000 home on a

14
00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:00.640
30-year fixed-rate mortgage. Their payments are set at $1,500 per month. Mary decides to

15
00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:05.040
protect her mortgage with what is known as a mortgage protection plan. Super creative

16
00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.640
name, right? She gets a 30-year plan in place to cover her 30-year mortgage at $250,000

17
00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.560
of protection. Larry, on the other hand, decides to spend that money on a subscription

18
00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:21.120
to the Cookie of the Month Club. Way to go, Larry. As the years pass, both Larry and Mary

19
00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.280
not each other. They're twins. That would be super weird. They start families,

20
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.600
get promotions, and all that good stuff. One day, Larry chokes on the double pistachio

21
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.800
chocolate chip from his Cookie of the Month Club and sadly dies. This is actually doubly sad

22
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.080
because the money he was spending on that cookie club could have been funding his mortgage

23
00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.840
protection plan that he never got. So Larry's wife is now stuck trying to make mortgage

24
00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.440
payments on her own, which she can't do now that the family's income has been cut in half.

25
00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.440
She slips into foreclosure and the family loses their home, all because Larry had to

26
00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.520
have his cookies. Now, if he would have gotten the mortgage protection plan that Mary has,

27
00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.000
Larry's family would have received the full $250,000 and a tax-free check from their

28
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.320
mortgage protection plan. The home would be paid off in full with money left to spare.

29
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:06.000
In addition, if something goes sideways with Mary's health, like a heart attack, stroke,

30
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.080
or cancer, her mortgage protection plan can be tapped into while she's still living,

31
00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.680
giving her crucial money to help pay the mortgage, or any other bills for that matter,

32
00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.560
while she's sick and out of work. Makes a lot of sense, right?

33
00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.600
Moral of this story, don't be a greedy, cookie-eating monster like Larry. If you have

34
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.920
a mortgage and you're making monthly payments, do the smart thing and protect that investment

35
00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.480
with a mortgage protection plan. You'll rest easy knowing that your most prized assets

36
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.080
are protected. And hey, those cookies were just going to go straight to your hips anyway.
